+
+The migration Job uses a migration-specific empty affinity by default so a
+pre-install cannot depend on a serving pod that does not exist yet. Capture its
+canonical report promptly: `ttlSecondsAfterFinished=3600` bounds completed
+Job/Pod retention. After terminal evidence capture, revoke/remove the migration
+Secret and explicitly delete the migration Job and NetworkPolicy; Helm hook
+resources are not ordinary release resources and the NetworkPolicy has no TTL.
+Target-cluster TTL-controller, scheduler, RuntimeClass, and CNI behavior remain
+live qualification gates.
+
+The onboarding evaluator is intentionally not a startup authority: live checks
+may need the deployed service to exist. First render the final production
+values and read the computed config digest from the
+`lightwork.daybreak.ai/production-deployment-config-sha256` annotation. Have the
+external evidence authority sign an observations manifest binding that exact
+digest, deployment URN, source revision, contract digest, and release-state
+digest. Stage it in the pre-provisioned Secret, bump
+`secret.rotationGeneration`, and recreate the pod so the init container takes
+one immutable owner-only snapshot. Then emit the report without mutating config:
+
+```bash
+kubectl exec deployment/maverick -- maverick production-onboarding-readiness
+```
+
+The command reads the fixed staged observations path and chart-injected
+out-of-band pins. A ready report still requires an external cross-evaluation
+nonce-consumption ledger; the in-process evaluator is stateless and rejects
+duplicates only within one manifest.
+
+`values-production.yaml` enables a chart-level fail-closed gate. Rendering is
+refused unless the release uses an immutable digest, a pre-provisioned Secret,
+a non-secret rotation generation,
+an operator-selected deployment URN, exact tagged source/contract/release-state
+digests, an independently trusted Ed25519 authority key ID/public key, and the
+fixed staged observations key,
+an exact drained migration authorization, separately custodied owner DSN, and
+database-only migration egress CIDR,
+Postgres with RLS, the mandatory enterprise startup preflight, a read-only root
+filesystem, persistent state, health probes, authenticated TLS ingress,
+namespace-restricted ingress, exact DNS resolver CIDRs, restricted dependency
+egress, non-root identity, RuntimeDefault seccomp, dropped Linux capabilities,
+no privilege escalation, finite CPU/memory/ephemeral-storage requests and
+limits, bounded `/tmp`, and exactly one control-plane replica. It also pins the first supported surface to vLLM, a
+gVisor-isolated control-plane pod, OIDC (or an explicitly selected trusted
+proxy), principal-isolated tenants, and a sandbox backend that refuses every
+arbitrary shell/code command. Ambiguous effects also require bounded
+reconciliation/escalation deadlines, an exact incident target, and a non-empty
+authenticated-adjudicator allowlist. The shared tenant quota authority requires
+one positive monotonic `tenantQuota.policyGeneration` plus exactly one policy
+source: all six scalar ceilings, or a complete strict
+`tenantQuota.limitsJSON` document with every scalar left empty. The chart emits
+`MAVERICK_TENANT_QUOTA_MAX_STORAGE_BYTES` with the scalar form. The Helm JSON
+environment entry is bounded to 64 KiB and must include a complete six-resource default; runtime
+readiness performs the full strict parse before the first tenant exists. See
+[`tenant-quota-contract.md`](../../docs/enterprise/tenant-quota-contract.md).
+Shared operator tokens, local invites, hosted
+providers, mutation tools, plugins, channels, RAG, and autonomous DGM are not
+admitted. The pod disables service-account-token projection.
+
+The projection is a key allowlist, not a bulk Secret mount. A broader
+pre-provisioned Secret may contain unrelated keys, but only the database, Vault,
+vLLM, wrapped-audit-key, and selected OIDC files named by the template reach the
+application custody snapshot. Raw audit private keys, cloud/Docker/Kubernetes/
+SSH credentials, static dashboard tokens, and arbitrary production `env`
+overrides are refused. The PID-1 launcher also verifies the read-only root,
+exact `/tmp`/state/secret mounts, absent host/control-plane paths, and fixed
+process/file and per-goal ceilings described in
+[`docs/enterprise/production-runtime-contract.md`](../../docs/enterprise/production-runtime-contract.md).
+RuntimeClass, CNI NetworkPolicy, CSI capacity, and cgroup shutdown behavior
+still require qualification on the target cluster; rendering the chart is not
+evidence that those external controls operated. Tenant quota enforcement also
+requires live Postgres concurrency, failover, recovery, and load qualification;
+the chart and repository tests do not supply that external evidence.
+
+The model values are deployment assertions, not an approval mechanism. Every
+field must match one current `approved` entry in the immutable
+`release/production-model-policy.json` embedded in the image: canonical model
+identifier, artifact digest, credential-free HTTPS endpoint, region, retention
+mode, mounted-file credential source, spend ceiling/period, and exact failover
+chain. Startup reads the vLLM key from the staged Secret, rejects config or
+environment bypass, and refuses policy, endpoint, model, artifact, custody, or
+cap drift before constructing a provider client. The checked-in policy is a
+draft with no admitted model; an evidence owner and independent security owner
+must approve real deployment facts before a production release can start.
+
+The production overlay enables a Prometheus Operator `ServiceMonitor`. Both the
+pod and the scraper receive `MAVERICK_METRICS_TOKEN` from the referenced Secret;
+startup fails if it is missing, weak, or reused. For a no-gap rotation: first
+put the new value in the overlap key `MAVERICK_METRICS_TOKEN_PREVIOUS` while
+leaving the old current value in place, bump `secret.rotationGeneration`, and
+recreate the pod. Then set
+`serviceMonitor.bearerTokenSecret.scrapeKey=MAVERICK_METRICS_TOKEN_PREVIOUS`
+and prove the new value scrapes. Swap the Secret values so the new value is
+current and the old value is previous, bump the generation and recreate the
+pod, switch `scrapeKey` back to `MAVERICK_METRICS_TOKEN`, prove it, and finally
+remove the old overlap value. Both credentials are accepted throughout the
+overlap, but the supported single-replica `Recreate` strategy has a planned
+availability interruption; it does not claim zero-downtime pod overlap. A
+previous key by itself is rejected.
+
+The checked-in `0.1.7` source manifest is deliberately marked release-ineligible.
+Until a signed release evidence packet flips that state, the runtime preflight
+will refuse to start this profile even when Helm renders successfully.
