+| `control_plane_lease_owned` | `1` | Resolve the single-writer owner. Do not scale dashboard/control-plane replicas. |
+| `postgres_rls_verified` | `1` | Verify `ENABLE` plus `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` and the exact fail-closed tenant policy on every scoped table. |
+| `transport_tls_verified` | `1` | Require the production ingress-TLS assertion, PostgreSQL `sslmode=verify-full` plus negotiated TLS, and verified TLS for non-loopback Redis. |
+| `indeterminate_side_effects` | `0` since process start | Reconcile the target system and signed receipt/audit chain before any retry. |
+| `queue_pending` | at most `100` | Check dispatcher/worker drain and capacity. Scale remote workers only. |
+| `queue_dead_letter`, `queue_stale_leases` | `0` | Preserve job evidence; a lease is stale after one hour. Reconcile effects before reclaim/retry. |
+| `kill_switch_clear` | `1` | Keep traffic stopped until the incident owner confirms it is safe to clear. |
+| `policy_integrity`, `policy_fallbacks` | integrity `1`, fallbacks `0` | Repair config/governance/runtime-overrides sources. Failed-closed actions must not be manually bypassed. |
+
+### SIEM outbox operation
+
+Run one tenant-scoped drain loop from the deployment scheduler; do not run
+competing ad-hoc exporters over the same tenant log. The command claims a
+bounded batch, requires a complete HTTPS collector acknowledgement, and leaves
+every unacknowledged batch encrypted in the outbox:
+
+```sh
+maverick audit siem-outbox status --tenant TENANT --fail-on-backlog
+maverick audit siem-outbox drain --tenant TENANT --limit 100 --timeout 10
+```
+
+Page on any dead-letter count. Preserve the collector and Lightwork evidence,
+determine whether the stable delivery id was already acknowledged remotely,
+and repair authentication/TLS/schema/capacity before redrive. Preview first,
+then explicitly authorize the same opaque delivery ids; redrive never changes
+the sealed payload, destination, or collector idempotency key:
+
+```sh
+maverick audit siem-outbox redrive --tenant TENANT --all-dead --limit 100 --dry-run
+maverick audit siem-outbox redrive --tenant TENANT --all-dead --limit 100 --yes
+maverick audit siem-outbox drain --tenant TENANT --limit 100 --timeout 10
+```
+
+Use repeated `--delivery-id <sha256>` instead of `--all-dead` when an incident
+has approved only specific batches. A redrive is itself written to the signed
+tenant audit chain before queue state changes; an unavailable required audit
+path refuses the operation. Do not delete or edit the SQLite outbox manually.
+
