+After the first supported release, removal or incompatible reinterpretation of
+an admitted operation requires all of the following:
+
+1. publish the deprecation in a supported release and start the clock there;
+2. keep the old behavior for at least 90 calendar days and two supported minor
+   releases, using the longer window;
+3. publish release notes and a concrete old-to-new request/response migration
+   example;
+4. bump and review the OpenAPI contract version and refresh the claim-evidence
+   ledger; and
+5. retain contract tests for the old behavior until the declared removal
+   release.
+
+Emergency removal of an unsafe operation is a security response, not a silent
+compatibility exception: the release must identify the security rationale,
+affected versions, replacement or containment path, and customer notification.
