+## Execution and external-effect guarantees
+
+Lightwork does not promise universal exactly-once execution. A queue claim has
+one winner for the current ready row, but crash recovery and lease expiry can
+deliver the job again. Handlers that can change an external system must use a
+stable provider idempotency key, reconcile by authoritative provider evidence,
+or stop in `INDETERMINATE`; an ambiguous operation must never be blindly
+retried.
+
+The authoritative `PREPARED`, `COMMITTED`, `REFUSED`, and `INDETERMINATE`
+contract, including the precise scope of the concurrency soak, is in
+[`specs/external-effect-semantics.md`](specs/external-effect-semantics.md).
+
+### Resolve an `INDETERMINATE` flow run
+
+1. Keep the run quarantined. `POST /api/v1/flows/runs/{id}/retry` returns 409
+   and no worker may repeat the original action.
+2. As the run owner, `GET /api/v1/flows/runs/{id}` and inspect
+   `indeterminate_case`. It contains bounded state/input/node commitments, the
+   failing node, reconciliation and escalation deadlines, the configured
+   escalation target, and the required operator actions. Preserve the provider
+   logs and related records outside Lightwork; put only opaque references and
+   a SHA-256 commitment in the resolution request.
+3. Query the provider's authoritative operation/ledger API using the original
+   idempotency key or external reference. Do not discover state by submitting
+   the mutation again. If a corrective or compensating action is needed, run it
+   as a separately approved operation and retain its reference.
+4. A tenant admin who is also named in
+   `MAVERICK_INDETERMINATE_ADJUDICATORS` submits
+   `POST /api/v1/flows/runs/{id}/resolve-indeterminate` with a unique
+   32-lowercase-hex `resolution_id`, one of `committed`, `not_committed`,
+   `compensated`, or `accepted_loss`, the reconciliation method and summary,
+   one to twenty opaque evidence references, `evidence_sha256`, an explicit
+   compensating-action statement, and any external reference. The record is
+   immutable; a different second resolution is refused.
+5. Set `replacement_authorized=true` only with a `not_committed` disposition
+   backed by authoritative evidence. That exact combination unlocks a fresh
+   admin-requested retry. Every other disposition remains non-retryable.
+
+The server writes `flow_indeterminate_resolved` to the required signed audit
+chain before publishing the resolution. If audit custody is unavailable, the
+resolution is not applied. Replaying the same `resolution_id` and exact request
+is idempotent. Resolution after the reconciliation/escalation deadline records
+the timeout/escalation flags permanently.
