+### Production onboarding is a separate fail-closed report
+
+`maverick init`, `maverick onboard`, the installer wizard, and both ordinary
+`preflight` profiles prepare or inspect an evaluation environment. They are not
+a production-readiness attestation. In particular, they do not prove the exact
+model policy, external identity mapping, deployed isolation runtime, Shield
+boundary, audit-key custody, live PostgreSQL and migration state, egress/TLS,
+secret rotation, quota saturation behavior, observability, or operational
+drills for a release.
+
+Use the signed release's production-onboarding contract, exact release-state
+bytes, and a trusted-authority-signed evidence manifest instead. The runtime
+must receive the expected contract/release-state SHA-256 values, exact source
+revision, stable deployment ID, exact normalized deployment/configuration
+SHA-256, authority key ID, and Ed25519 public key through independently
+controlled deployment configuration; a target identity or key disclosed only
+by the evidence file is never authority.
+
+The production Helm overlay wires these independent pins directly into the pod.
+It computes the deployment-config digest from canonical JSON for the merged
+runtime-relevant values (excluding only the separately bound onboarding block
+and Secret rollout generation), fixes the observations path under the immutable
+staged Secret snapshot, and rejects missing, zero, malformed, or redirected
+pins before rendering. Read the computed digest from the
+`lightwork.daybreak.ai/production-deployment-config-sha256` annotation, have the
+external authority bind it in the signed manifest, stage the observations key,
+and recreate the pod with a new Secret generation. The ordinary Helm install
+does not turn that evidence into a startup self-attestation.
+
+```bash
+maverick production-onboarding-readiness \
+  --contract /etc/lightwork/production-onboarding-contract.json \
+  --release-state /etc/lightwork/release-state.json \
+  --observations ./signed-exact-release-evidence.json
+```
+
+The machine-readable report records `pass`, `fail`, or `not_checked` for every
+required domain. Omitting `--observations` deliberately reports every live
+requirement as `not_checked`. A required failure, unknown, expired observation,
+missing per-requirement evidence, invalid signature, duplicate/replayed
+evidence artifact, contract/release-state digest mismatch, untrusted or zero
+revision, deployment-target mismatch, or an ineligible release contract exits
+nonzero. The signature covers the exact canonical manifest bytes, including
+the deployment ID/configuration digest and every result and evidence digest.
+`maverick init --production` is a report-only alias: it refuses `--fast`,
+`--resume`, and `--from-file`, never writes installer configuration, and ends
+with this same report. Omitting observations exits nonzero.
+
+Duplicate evidence IDs and artifact tuples are rejected within one manifest.
+The evaluator is stateless, so consuming a nonce across separate evaluations
+requires an external deployment-authority ledger; this command does not claim
+global one-shot replay prevention. The command is read-only and makes no
+network calls; it validates supplied evidence but cannot prove an unsupplied
+live fact or confer legal certification.
