+The committed ratchet contains 91 reviewed failure identities from the measured
+``packages/maverick-core/tests`` secure-default run. That reviewed identity set
+is the point of this module. It is scoped to maverick-core because that is where
+every control the posture flips lives, and because that is the tree the baseline
+was actually measured over -- widening the claim to the whole workspace without
+measuring it would be the defect this repo keeps finding. The entries are
+reviewed debt, not evidence that the secure posture passes: they currently
+represent legacy-default assertions and fixtures that do not provision the
+controls enabled by that posture.
